  "problem": "Write the space $R$ bounded by the cylinder as a type I region in three-dimensional space.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $R={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,y)\\in D,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,\\le z\\le \\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$},$ where\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-3}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,1}.$",
  "worked_solution": "A typical three-dimensional type I region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14094056/assets/05f940e247c6cd5d862d81fc3a34658353bef5513dfe862bbc67a120c0345838.png)\n\nFirst, we have that $z$ is bounded below by $0$ and above by $3.$ So, the type I representation of $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,y)\\in D,\\,0\\le z\\le 3\\,}.\n$$\n\nNow, that base curve in the $xy$-plane of the cylinder's surface is the circle $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1$ centered at $(0,0).$ Therefore, the domain $D$ is given by the following disc:\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}\\,\\,\\le \\,\\,1}.\n$$",
